# DonorLink UG: Phase 3 (Booking with Capacity Control) Walkthrough

This walkthrough documents the architecture, database migrations, atomic capacity control, concurrency proofs, and verification procedures for **Phase 3: Booking with Capacity Control** for **Uganda Blood Transfusion Services (UBTS)**.

---

## 1. System Architecture & Atomic Booking Data Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Donor as Voluntary Donor
    participant Web as Web Routes / Controller
    participant Svc as BookingService
    participant DB as Database (SQLite / Postgres / MySQL)
    participant Evt as Event Bus (Post-Commit)

    Note over Donor,Evt: Booking a Donation Slot with Atomic Capacity Reservation
    Donor->>Web: POST /donor/appointments (slot_id)
    Web->>Svc: book(donor, slot)
    
    activate Svc
    Svc->>DB: DB::transaction(callback, attempts: 10)
    Svc->>DB: Lock User row: SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ? FOR UPDATE
    Svc->>Svc: Validate donor is active, verified, drive published, slot not past/cutoff
    Svc->>DB: Check existing booked appointment on this drive (max 1 per drive)
    
    Note over Svc,DB: Atomic Reserve (Never Read-Then-Write)
    Svc->>DB: UPDATE slots SET booked_count = booked_count + 1 WHERE id = ? AND booked_count < capacity
    alt Zero rows affected (Slot Full)
        DB-->>Svc: 0 rows updated
        Svc-->>Web: throws SlotFullException("That slot has just been filled. Please choose another time.")
        Web-->>Donor: Redirects back with friendly error banner
    else Place Reserved (1 row updated)
        DB-->>Svc: 1 row updated
        Svc->>DB: INSERT INTO appointments (user_id, slot_id, status='booked')
        Svc->>DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION
        Svc->>Evt: dispatch(new AppointmentBooked(appointment)) [After Commit]
        Svc-->>Web: returns Appointment
        Web-->>Donor: Redirects to /donor/appointments with confirmation banner
    end
    deactivate Svc
```

